<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hattusa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hattusa was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>, located near present-day Boğazkale in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. The site has yielded large archives of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> tablets, monumental gates and temples. It was abandoned and destroyed during the collapse of the Hittite state around the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hattusa.jpg" alt="Hattusa" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carole Raddato from FRANKFURT, Germany · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lion_Gate,_Hattusa_13_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
